{"id":"G1080","lemma":"γεννάω","transliteration":"gennaō","sayIt":"gennaō","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"verb","gloss":"to beget","meaning":"γεννάω, -ῶ\n(γέννα, poët. for γένος), [in LXX chiefly for ילד ;]\n1. of the father, to beget: with accusative, Mat.1:1-16, Act.7:8, 29; before ἐκ, Mat.1:3, 5, 6.\n2. Of the mother, to bring forth, bear: Luk.1:13, 57 23:29, Jhn.16:21; εἰς δουλείαν, Gal.4:24. Pass.\n(1) to be begotten: Mat.1:20;\n(2) to be born: Mat.2:1, 4 19:12 26:24, Mrk.14:21, Luk.1:35, Jhn.3:4, Act.7:20, Rom.9:11, Heb.11:23; before εἰς, Jhn.16:21 18:37, 2Pe.2:12; ἐν, Act.2:8 22:3, (ἁμαρτίαις), Jhn.9:34; ἀπό, Heb.11:12 (WH, mg., ἐγεν-); ἐκ, Jhn.1:13 3:6 8:41; with adj., τυφλὸς γ., Jhn.9:2; [Ῥωμαῖος ], Act.22:28; κατὰ σάρκα: κ. πνεῦμα: Gal.4:29. Metaphorical; μάχας, 2Ti.2:23; ὑμᾶς ἐγέννησα, 1Co.4:15, (ὅν), Phm 10; in quotation, Psa.2:7 (LXX), Act.13:33, Heb.1:5 5:5; of Christians as begotten of God, born again: Jhn.1:13 3:3, 5-8, 1Jn.2:29 3:9 4:7 5:1, 4, 18 (cf. ἀνα-γεννάω); (Cremer, 146).\n(AS)","glosses":["born","father of","have become your father","has been born","had not been born","conceived"],"count":65,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"mat-1","v":2,"renderings":{"bsb":"was the father of","kjv":"begat"}},{"chapterId":"mat-1","v":3,"renderings":{"bsb":"was the father of","kjv":"begat"}},{"chapterId":"mat-1","v":4,"renderings":{"bsb":"was the father of","kjv":"begat"}},{"chapterId":"mat-1","v":5,"renderings":{"bsb":"was the father of","kjv":"begat"}},{"chapterId":"mat-1","v":6,"renderings":{"bsb":"the father of","kjv":"begat"}},{"chapterId":"mat-1","v":7,"renderings":{"bsb":"the father of","kjv":"begat"}},{"chapterId":"mat-1","v":8,"renderings":{"bsb":"was the father of","kjv":"begat"}},{"chapterId":"mat-1","v":9,"renderings":{"bsb":"was the father of","kjv":"begat"}},{"chapterId":"mat-1","v":10,"renderings":{"bsb":"was the father of","kjv":"begat"}},{"chapterId":"mat-1","v":11,"renderings":{"bsb":"the father of","kjv":"begat"}},{"chapterId":"mat-1","v":12